SUMMARY:A Three Mountains "Battle of the Bands"
DESCRIPTION:This is a Rock and Roll themed\, team melee and bardic camping 
 event.\n\nhttps://antirsca.wixsite.com/battlebands \n \nThere will be priz
 es for the winning melee team AND bardic competitions to be held AND a win
 ners feast.\n\nThe Melee tournament will be of teams of 5 combatants and b
 e held in the medieval style with galleries for spectators and crowd invol
 vement!&nbsp; \n\nEach Melee “band” will also be required to have a Bard o
 r Herald to introduce/ hype/ herald the team onto the field each time. (th
 ink Chaucer from the movie Knights Tale…)&nbsp; \nThis will be one of the tw
 o bardic competitions\, the Best Intro or Field Presence.&nbsp; The second Bar
 dic competition would be held during the Winners feast and be a performanc
 e composed or written about something the bard had seen during the days me
 lee competition..\n\nThere will be a feast with a head table for the Winni
 ng team and visiting royalty.&nbsp; This will be prepared family style by the 
 VC with service for the Head table on Saturday night after the tournament.
 \n\nOn Friday and Saturday night we’d like to host “Open Mic night” 
 which would be a torch light/ Pas d’ Arm/ barrier tournament (with Prize
 s) AND combination Rock and Roll Karaoke.&nbsp;&nbsp;\nCall it “Friday Night\, o
 pen-mike\, Pas d’ Arme and Karaoke”\n\nThis will be a weekend camping 
 event and support RVs\n\nhttps://antirsca.wixsite.com/battlebands\n\nSched
 ule\nFriday\nNoon - Gate open for volunteers\n3pm - Gate opens to public\n
 6pm - VC serves dinner\n8pm (darkish) - 10pm - Torchlight Karaoke and Barr
 ier Pas d’ Arm\nMidnight - Quiet please\n\n\nSaturday\n8am - Gate opens\
 n9am - announcements - Armor Inspection\n10am Battle of the Band Melee Tou
 rnament begins\nNoon - 2pm Lunch break at the VC\n2pm - Tournament resumes
  if needed\n2pm 3M Legacy Champions Raiper scroll Tournament\n6pm - VC Din
 ner and Prize Court\, Bardic competition for best original piece\n Midnigh
 t - Quiet please\n\n\nSunday\nNoon - Site closes\n\n&nbsp;\;
CATEGORIES:Three Mountains
LOCATION:Bear Creek Tree Farm\, 30300 S Elisha Rd\, Molalla\, OR\, 97038\, 
 Rivers\, United States
