URL:https://antir.org/events/barons-ball-14/
SUMMARY:Baron's Ball
DESCRIPTION:Good gentles all! Lend ye to the call of your Baron! Long do th
 e nights begin to grow as summer gives way to autumn's cold. Join us for t
 he final camping event of the season at Baron's Ball! Defend the honor of 
 your Baron and Barony in war! Scenarios TBD. If war isn't your thing\, com
 pete to become Wastekeep's next Arts and Sciences champion or Bardic champ
 ion. Have a twisted mind and way with words? Compete for the honor of beco
 ming Wastekeep's next Defenestrator!\n\nYouth! Our Baron calls for your ai
 d as well! Test your creativity in the annual Veggie Creature Creation Com
 petition. Show off your prowess in Youth Armored Combat and Youth Armored 
 Rapier competitions!\n\nHospitality more your speed? Join us for our hospi
 tality competition.\n\n\n\nPlease contact Magdi Tynkere with questions.\n\
 n\nReservations\nLarge camping groups and RVs please contact Magdi for res
 ervations. Smaller groups should have plenty of space for camping. There a
 re no RV hookups\, so please plan on self-containment. Contact her with yo
 ur SCA name and the length of your RV.\n\nDetails of Competitions &amp;\; A
 ctivities\nWastekeep Arts &amp;\; Sciences Championship - The Kids Are Alri
 ght\n\nFor millennia\, older generations have complained about the younger
  generation. But as time marched forward\, progress and human ingenuity pe
 rsevered. There can only be one conclusion:\nThe kids are alright.\n\n\n\n
 We as SCAdians see this very clearly\, as we care for and nurture younger 
 generations\, and focus an passing down knowledge and wisdom. This is espe
 cially apparent in our legacy SCAdians. So to honor this (and as a nod to 
 our Queen and Royal Princess)\, let's acknowledge the importance of the yo
 unger generation.\n\n\n\nPlease bring an item (or items if you wish) that 
 have something to do with the youth. It could be games\, clothing\, kits f
 or kids to learn\, art forms about kids\, art by kids\, or anything that y
 ou can use to tell a story about special youth in your life.\n\n\n\nPopula
 ce judging\, and the youth of An Tir are encouraged to help judge\, as the
  future of our populace.\n\nWastebeast Arts &amp;\; Sciences Competition\n\
 nLong ago\, at the beginning of time in Wastekeep\, there was a story abou
 t the Wastebeast. The Beast of Wastekeep. That story\, once for\, has been
  found\, but alas no drawing of this wonderful beast remains. We are hopin
 g to change this and ask a boon of An Tir. Please help us revive this beas
 t\, by submitting your rendition of our magnificent creature to the popula
 ce at Barons Ball. A contest to spark creativity\, and based on the story
 ’s description:\n\n\n\nA most marvelous crew like a dragon and like a gr
 iffin and like a hydra\, but none of these. The skin is emerald green and 
 the scales shine like bronze. The claws and mouths are blood-red\, and the
 y have two heads\, one to sleep and one to watch.\n\n\nThe chosen entry wi
 ll be used in the future by artisans of Wastekeep\, so please be careful a
 nd do not use any copyright drawings. Have fun with this and looking forwa
 rd to all the creative idea. Please direct questions to Ciosa Fioravanti.\
 nLargesse Competition\n\n\n(Please read to the rhyme of Baa Baa Black Shee
 p)\n\n\n\nLargesse makers have you any wool?\nYes we do! Three bags full.\
 nOne for the Baronage\, one for the game\,\n and one for Her Magesty to sh
 are down the lane.\n\n\nIt’s a three item largesse contest\, and it does
  not need to be made of wool. Each entrant will receive one of the submitt
 ed largesse items\, others divided between kingdom and barony. Please dire
 ct questions to Ciosa Fioravanti.\nBaby Shower for the Princess Royale\n(S
 eparate Facebook Event located here.)\n\nThere are events of importance th
 at are told in stars. The birth of a Royal Princess is one such event. To 
 welcome her into the embrace of the House of Jarlskald and Argent Fox\, th
 e Barony of Wastekeep and the Kingdom of An Tir\, a vigil (aka baby shower
 ) is planned for Baron’s Ball\, October 2nd. Those who would like to con
 tribute food items please note that as the Princess Royal is a ray of suns
 hine\, and to honor the Queen’s preference\, sweet or savory lemon items
  including beverages or other savory snacks are appreciated.\nActivities a
 re planned!\nWords of Wisdom and Encouragement – Please share your wisdo
 m\, skills acquired and experiences in the vigil book or on a note card. P
 erhaps a cautionary tale of things you learned the hard way? Baby Doll Clo
 thes –The Jarlskald Raiding and Trading Company recently returned from a
  successful venture with an entire basket of naked baby dolls!! Clearly th
 ese babies need garments! There are 13 babies in all. Her Majesty will sel
 ect one for the Princess along with a few outfits. The generous Princess R
 oyal will be donated the rest to largesse. Baby Doll measurements are in t
 he comments below. If you are unable to attend Baron’s Ball garments may
  be sent via mail or another party. Message one of the Vigil Hosts for an 
 address.Diaper Toss – Accurate disposal of diapers is a must for all. De
 monstrate your skill by tossing the most diapers into a target. The winner
  will receive a prize of the lemon variety.We are looking forward to seein
 g one and all at their Majesties last event until the biggest event of all
 \, the birth of the Princess!!\n\n\n\n
CATEGORIES:Inlands Region,Kingdom of An Tir,Wastekeep
LOCATION:Basin City Memorial Park and Arena\, 303 Bailie Blvd\, Mesa\, WA\,
  99343\, Inland\, United States
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=303 Bailie Blvd\, Mesa\, WA
 \, 99343\, Inland\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Basin City Me
 morial Park and Arena:geo:0,0
END:VEVENT
