URL:https://antir.org/events/harvest-feast-51/
SUMMARY:Harvest Feast
DESCRIPTION:This is a Level 2: Branch Event where no Kingdom or Principalit
 y business is expected to be conducted event.\n\n10:00 AM8:00 PM\nTheir Ex
 cellencies\, Baroness&nbsp;Furia Dommitia and Baron&nbsp;Conrad Cedricson\, invite
  all to vie for Their Arts and Sciences\, Youth Arts &amp;\; Sciences\, &amp;am
 p\; Bardic Champions! Harvest Feast will also include Scholar’s Presenta
 tions\, martial practices\, and hand crafts. The all-day-long feast theme 
 is&nbsp;El Pasado Presente!\, the present past – Spanish Cuisine!\n\nMany ha
 nds make light work\, and as such Their Excellencies\, along with the rest
  of the Financial Committee\, wish to pass on the fruits of your hard work
  at making June Faire a huge success this year. As a thank you they have d
 ecided that Harvest Feast will be FREE for all who attend.\n\n\n\n\n\nFeas
 t is limited to 120 so you must be pre-registered to ensure your spot.&nbsp;Pl
 ease fill out the form for each person in your party.\n\n\n\nEvent team me
 mbers:\nEvent Steward: Lyleth Ó hAllmhuráin\n\nFeast Coordinator: Lord R
 owyn MacLost\nPre-registration and Accessibility: THL Jessy Gateman\, Dr
 agonsLaire.PreReg@antir.org\nArts &amp;\; Sciences and Bardic Championship 
 Coordinator: THL Karl inn irski\, THL Ciar ingen Fiachnae: DragonsLaire.
 ArtNSci@antir.org\nScholar’s Coordinator: THL Rycheza z Polska\nYouth Ac
 tivities: Lady Pak Sol Hwa\nWebminister: Lady Kira&nbsp;Kirova\, DragonsLair
 e.Webminister@antir.org\nSocial Media: THL Caterina da Savona\, DragonsL
 aire.SocialMedia@antir.org\nDecorations: THL Sigridr Vilhjalmsdottir\n\nOt
 her sites for event info:\nBaronial event link: https://dragonslaire.antir
 .org/wordpress/events/harvest-feast/\nFacebook event link:&nbsp;https://www.fa
 cebook.com/events/2117668175814901\n\n\n\nWhere? When?\nWhen: October 10\,
  2026. The hall opens at 8AM for setup — 10AM for everyone else. The hal
 l closes at 8PM.\n\nWhere:&nbsp;Key Peninsula Civic Center at 17010 S Vaughn R
 d NW\, Vaughn\, WA 98394 (link to Google map).\n\nParking: Please only par
 k in the front Civic Center parking lot. Do not park on private property\,
  or in the back of the Civic Center.\n\n\n\n\n\nBaronial Court\nBaroness&nbsp;
 Furia Dommitia and Baron&nbsp;Conrad Cedricson will preside over opening court
  in the morning (time TBA). Competitors for the A&amp;\;S and Bardic Champi
 onships should be prepared to stand up and declare their intent!\n\nThe wi
 nners will be announced at Evening Court (time TBA)\, as will the Scholars
  of Dragon’s Laire\, and there will be other awards for various members 
 of the Barony.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSchedule\nThe schedule will be posted 
 here when available.\n\n8AM: site opens for set-up\n10AM: site opens for t
 he general populace\n8PM: site closes\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPeople intera
 cting with this event must adhere to the SCA Core values\; behave with cou
 rtesy\, honor\, chivalry and respect\, even in times of inevitable differe
 nces of opinion\; and comply with SCA policy and modern law. The SCA prohi
 bits harassment and bullying of all individuals and groups. Hate speech is
  not tolerated in the Society. Hate speech is speech or symbols that offen
 d\, threaten\, or insult individuals or groups\, based on race\, color\, r
 eligion\, national origin\, sexual orientation\, disability or other trait
 s.\n\n\n
CATEGORIES:Dragon's Laire,Kingdom of An Tir,Western Region
LOCATION:Key Peninsula Civic Center\, 17010 South Vaughn Road NW\, Vaughn\,
  WA\, 98394\, Western\, United States
