URL:https://antir.org/events/crows-feast-2026/
SUMMARY:Crows' Feast 2026
DESCRIPTION:This is a Level 2: Branch Event where no Kingdom or Principalit
 y business is expected to be conducted event.\n\n10:00 AM7:00 PM\n\nAdditi
 onal information at the Facebook Event\n\nFriends\, the rustling of wings 
 and rattling of wind bid you welcome to the fantastic fete: Crows gather a
 t our Gate to welcome those from near and far. Come join us for a day of s
 tory\, games\, dancing\, tasty foods and more.\n\nSite opens at 10 am and 
 closes at 7 pm. Feast will begin at 3 am with court to follow. A wheelchai
 r ramp is available.\n\nGate\nAdults - $25*\nYouth (13-18) - $10**\nChildr
 en Feast (12 and under) - Free\n\nPreregister here\n\n*Adult SCA members w
 ill receive a $10 discount off the pricing above. Membership Number and Ex
 piration Date must be provided to receive the discount.\n**Registering chi
 ldren is no charge\, but will speed up the entry process. Youth and Childr
 en must either be accompanied by parent/guardian or their parent or guardi
 an must complete both of the SCA Inc. required forms prior to your arrival
 : Minor Waiver and Medical Authorization.\n\nActivities\nTheir Excellencie
 s of Glymm Mere will hold baronial court.\n\nMenu will include charcuterie
 \, fresh bread\, pottage\, and light dessert. The main dish will be gluten
  and dairy free\, with a vegan option available (items with gluten will be
  prepped in the same area\, so exercise caution). A dessert auction will b
 enefit Greater Chehalis Food Bank\, a 501(c)(3) organization.\n\nContests!
 \nCraftiest Crow: a show and tell style A&amp;\;S Competition\, be the craf
 tiest among us!\nCrow of Crows: a bardic competition\, sign up for a 10 mi
 nute slot when you arrive\, crowing rights apply\nBenevolent Crow: largess
  competition\, donate two items for baronial largess - populace favorite w
 ins a donated item and a token of appreciation\n\nGames will be played\, c
 lasses will be held (dancing!)\, and with enough interest\, fighter/rapier
  practice may take place. There is some indoor space available. Contact th
 e Steward if you would like to teach or help.
CATEGORIES:Crows Gate
