URL:https://antir.org/events/three-mountains-honor-feast-2/
SUMMARY:Three Mountains Honor Feast
DESCRIPTION:This is a Level 1: Other (Branch primary events of regional or 
 Kingdom interest) event.\n\n 	10:00 AM9:00 AM\n\nThree Mountains Honor Fea
 st and Arts and Sciences Championship \nFee: $ 40.00 with members receivin
 g a $10.00 discount\nParking is limited\, carpooling is highly recommended
 \nCome join us for a day of feasting and classes in honor of Dame Be'akbel
 le of Dumfries. Dame Be'akbell is well know for her love of fibre arts and
  contributions to largesse and the classes planned reflect that love. The 
 food will cover from Lisbon to Morocco.  \n\nThe Arts and Sciences Champio
 nship is a large part of the event and has been designed to reflect Dame B
 e'akbell's interests: Competitors will be asked to submit two entries in t
 he following categories:\nBe'ak is a pillar of largesse making and organiz
 ing\, so the first entery is a delightful duo in a medium of the competito
 rs choice. This involes two high end items\, suitable to be given as prize
 s or high end largesse. Time to show off your creative prowess! ( Entrants
  will be allowed to pick an item from their competitors' duo to take home 
 in recognition of their hardwork)\nBe'ak's second passion is fiber arts an
 d requests the second entry to be a project based in the fibre arts. This 
 can include " classic" examples of fibre arts like sewing\, knitting\, wea
 ving etc but we would love to see creative interpetations.\nOur Honoree is
  a proud 14th century Scotswoman\, bonus points will be awarded to items t
 hat are 14th century or scottish in origin.\nJudges with be using the King
 dom's Arts and Sciences rubrics found here: www.baronyofthreemountains.org
 /documents/downloads/\nWe encourage you to consult the rubics to give the 
 best possible entry.\nThe deadline for Entry is October 10\, so that appro
 priate judges can be arranged. For further information or registration for
  comepition please contact : Anne Southworth\, our current baronial champi
 on.
CATEGORIES:Three Mountains
LOCATION:Eastgate Masonic Lodge\, 4812 NE 102nd\, Portland\, OR\, 97220\, R
 IVERS\, United States
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=4812 NE 102nd\, Portland\, 
 OR\, 97220\, RIVERS\, United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=100;X-TITLE=Eastgate Ma
 sonic Lodge:geo:0,0
END:VEVENT
