URL:https://antir.org/events/good-yule-2026/
SUMMARY:Good Yule 2026
DESCRIPTION:Site opens for event staff at 9am – gate for the populace wil
 l open at 10am and ends at 8pm.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nCome one\, come all good gen
 tles!\n\nYule is fast approaching\, and with that we invite you to come en
 joy the festivities. We will be having a Celtic theme this year. We're luc
 ky to have Aquaterra's own Oz Von Baekyn designing and preparing our glori
 ous feast. What tasty treats will she present to us? Of course\, Bardic an
 d A&amp;\;S championships will be happening. What stories and beauty will w
 e see and hear? As per tradition the dessert auction will be continuing wi
 th our donations going to Skagit Valley Humane Society. An amazing choice 
 showcasing the kindness of our Baron and Baroness. Bring your best baked g
 oods! The person with the highest selling goodie shall receive a delightfu
 l prize. The silent auction will be happening\, too. Please feel free to d
 onate and bid\, for the profits from this support An Tir’s Ravens travel
  fund. There will be some new fun too\, such as medieval bingo and best dr
 essed table competition. Yes\, there will be prizes!!! We will be taking s
 ome time to honor and celebrate Lóft Jólgeirson’s being the newest Chi
 valry Vigilant. We hope to see you all there to enjoy the feast\, the cama
 raderie of friends\, family\, and some new friends\, too.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nSi
 te Notes: \n\nThis site is ADA accessible.\n\nAlcohol will not be allowed 
 at this event.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nLinks for preregistration and volunteering wi
 ll be available soon!&nbsp;\n\n**Please note\, if you plan to attend the feast
 \, you MUST preregister (there is an extra $5 discount when you do)!! Day 
 trip attendance will only be available at the door with cash or check only
 !! All adult members receive a $10 discount.&nbsp;\n\nSite Fees\n\n\n\nFee Typ
 e **\nCost*\n\n\nAdult Feast\n$45\n\n\nYouth (12-17) Feast\n$15\n\n\nUnder
  12\nFree\n\n\nFamily Cap\n$120\n\n\nAdult Day NO Feast (cash or check at 
 door only)\n$20\n\n\nYouth/Child (Under 18) Day NO Feast\nFree\n\n\n\n\n*T
 here is a $5 discount on all feast tickets when you preregister.\n\n&nbsp;\
 ;\n** All adult members will get the $10 membership discount. Please bring
  proof of current membership to avoid being charged the $10 at the door.\n
 \n\n\n&nbsp;\n\nMeal Information – The menu will be posted as soon as availa
 ble. Lady Oz Von Baekyn will be accommodating for food allergies and dieta
 ry restrictions. There will be a space available in the prereg form that w
 ill allow you to share your allergies and restrictions.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nBard
 ic Championship Information \n\nRULES FOR IF YOU WIN:\n\n1) Be Prepared to
  BRING THE FUN\n\n 	a) Where ever you go\, try and do at least ONE THING t
 hat spreads joy. (Tell a joke\, lead a dance\, teach a silly game (Gurning
  comes to mind). Whistle a happy tune.\n 	b) State loudly and proudly that
  you are the Bardic Champion of the Great and Mighty Barony of Aquaterra!\
 n\n&nbsp;\;\n\n2) Wear the Regalia PROUDLY. (and try really\, really hard n
 ot to lose it).\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\n3) Be the Champion\, encourage Bardic Arts (
 and there are DOZENS AND DOZENS of them) as you can.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\n4) Show
  up at the event to choose your successor and help run the contest. Hand o
 ver the Regalia. Be a Bard.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nNow\, HOW DO I COMPETE TO BE CHA
 MPION???\n\n 	A) Show Up at Aquaterra Good Yule DECEMBER 5\, 2026\n\nB ) T
 ell me you are entering.\n\n 	C) Tell me WHAT you are doing to satisfy the
  CHALLENGES OF A BARD for C-1\, C-2\, &amp;\; C-3!\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nC-1) Do so
 me sort of Bardic "THING" (™) that makes people joyful! Like\, teaching 
 a dance or just play or sing or clap a jaunty song. Teach a MayPole (just 
 a suggestion).\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nC-2) Do some sort of Bardic "THING" (™) tha
 t helps relieve tension\, shed a tear\, touch feelings. (Lullaby\, Story\,
  Song\, Tune\, Poem...)\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nC-3) There will be an Improvisationa
 l Challenge. I will have a BUCKET OF MYSTERY there with many strange\, arc
 ane\, and odd objects in it. You may pick 2 or 3 objects and make up a son
 g\, story\, tune\, tale\, ... using those objects. Have fun.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\
 nBardic is like a LARGE Day Shade and can accommodate MANY an activity. Yo
 u are free to PM me for ideas\, for that\, too\, is part of a Bard's job\,
  to seek out information\, research\, and ask good questions.\n\n&nbsp;\;\n
 \nThe MAIN THINGS being looked for are:\n\nCONNECTION with the Audience. B
 E Your Persona and make the Audience feel SEEN.\n\nVERSATILITY of Performa
 nce Style (one _can_ play pennywhistle for all their entries\, but if you 
 can also do a speech\, lead a dance\, tell a story\, etc.\, that is even b
 etter.)\n\nBring the JOY! Try something New-ish. Have FUN!\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\nI
 n service to Crown\, Coronet\, and the Barony of Aquaterra.\n\nZahra\n\n&amp;n
 bsp\;\n\nA&amp;\;S Championship Information – more coming soon. \n\nJoy &amp;
 amp\; Dream – make something that brings you joy to share and spread joy
  to the dream. More details coming soon!\n\n&nbsp;\n\nDetails for the Best Dre
 ssed Table competition and An Tir Bingo will be coming soon!\n\n&nbsp;\;\n\
 nThis is a Level 2: Branch Event where no Kingdom or Principality business
  is expected to be conducted event.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\;
CATEGORIES:Aquaterra,Kingdom of An Tir,Western Region
